{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the proof-reuse semantics for request 7c0e8181, answering 2fd47b11.\n\nAdopt the multi-root room proof. One command-local verifier for `dap verify --all`: every requested scope of the room is a root at depth 0, foreign depth is the least distance from any root actually followed, and a prefix or content proven once in the run is a lemma for every later target that needs it. Cached proofs bind the exact source, incarnation, entry hash, and the semantic, code and trust options; nothing from discovery alone becomes proof; expected heads, causal-prefix checks, contradiction invalidation and failed-fold quarantine stay required. The run ends with one union coverage and trust record that names, for each shared prefix, the root under which it was proven, and with the per-scope summaries as today.\n\nStandalone `verify(source, options)` keeps its single-target semantics, and every existing test stays unchanged. Detached text settled from a checked source within the same run may serve another target under the same binding; the coverage record says so.\n\nThe contract gets a short clarification in section 9.4 of notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md: depth is from the nearest root of the proof, and a room proof has the requested scopes as its roots. The replay README says the same in one paragraph. Strict per-target fresh-traversal equivalence with conditional certificates is not required.\n\nDefaults, standalone results, real HTTP accounting and the accepted prior-head control stay unchanged. The 2,000-member run reports every actual scope consistent under shipped defaults. Order: 121a8913 (now in changes requested), then 7c0e8181, then J4.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}